<article class="env-lemma" id="2F816F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2F816F">Lemma <span data-tag="2F816F">2.4.6.4</span>.</a> Let $\calC \subseteq \calD $ be an inclusion of simplicial sets which is also a categorical equivalence. Suppose further that $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category. Then $\calC $ is a retract of $\calD $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Enlarging $\calD $ by an inner anodyne extension if necessary, we may suppose that $\calD $ is an $\infty $-category. We now apply Lemma <a href="/tag/547DD4" data-tag="547DD4">2.4.6.3</a> in the case where $A = \calC $, $B = \calD $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>